            <ArticleTitle>Usefulness of the admission electrocardiogram for identifying the infarct-related artery in inferior wall acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>182-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We analyzed the admission electrocardiogram in 109 patients with inferior wall acute myocardial infarction in an attempt to determine the infarct-related artery (IRA). The presence of ST depression in leads V1 or V2 had a high sensitivity for predicting the left circumflex artery as the IRA. The lack of ST depression in V1 or V2 had a high negative predictive value for excluding the left circumflex artery as the IRA.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
